WEBVTT

00:14.280 --> 00:16.720
Khaaghdshgfujikoropi…

00:16.720 --> 00:18.410
Were those even words?

00:18.600 --> 00:22.390
C-C-C-Can you blame me?! Look at all of them!

00:22.550 --> 00:26.200
All four of Furin's devas
are right in front of us!

00:27.250 --> 00:28.400
Who's what?

00:29.210 --> 00:30.700
Don't call them "what".

00:30.810 --> 00:32.000
O-Okay…

00:33.850 --> 00:36.480
The Jikoku Squad leader, Tsubakino.

00:37.340 --> 00:39.770
The Komoku Squad leader, Mizuki.

00:40.530 --> 00:43.110
The Zocho Squad leader, Momose.

00:44.010 --> 00:47.110
And Hiragi, the head of our very own Tamon Squad!

00:47.900 --> 00:50.600
These four are the very core of Bofurin!

00:51.590 --> 00:53.500
Thanks for coming here, guys.

00:53.960 --> 00:58.920
Going forward, everyone gathered
here will be leaders of Bofurin,

00:59.860 --> 01:03.410
but before that, there's something
I have to tell you all.

01:04.450 --> 01:06.740
Some of you may have already noticed, but…

01:08.840 --> 01:12.380
The replanting of this year's seedlings
went off without a hitch!

01:12.380 --> 01:12.900
Huh?

01:13.400 --> 01:13.810
[Smug]

01:13.820 --> 01:17.630
[Smug]
Sugishita there was a crazy-huge help!

01:17.910 --> 01:21.390
We've got more planters this year,
so there'll be loads to eat!

01:21.520 --> 01:24.380
Look forward to the summer barbecue competition!

01:24.760 --> 01:27.990
[Irritated]
Umemiya, is this really the time for that?

01:28.150 --> 01:32.000
Whaaat? We finished replanting,
of course I want them to see it.

01:32.090 --> 01:35.880
We got all the grade reps here,
so give them an address!

01:36.130 --> 01:37.640
An address?

01:38.130 --> 01:41.150
I didn't plan to do anything so pompous,

01:42.010 --> 01:43.650
but I guess I can say this.

01:44.600 --> 01:45.690
Hey, guys.

01:47.140 --> 01:48.330
Countin' on ya.

01:49.530 --> 01:52.330
I know there are limits to what I can do alone.

01:52.780 --> 01:57.610
It's impossible for me to keep
an eye on everyone in the school.

01:58.170 --> 02:00.510
That's why I want to leave that to you.

02:01.310 --> 02:04.200
Watch over the people around you,

02:04.480 --> 02:05.680
and help them!

02:08.360 --> 02:09.140
Please.

02:09.750 --> 02:10.770
Yes, sir!

02:20.190 --> 02:21.520
Alright, for now,

02:21.780 --> 02:23.990
do your meet-and-greets with your squad.

02:25.270 --> 02:28.220
So you were picked for our first-year grade rep!

02:28.840 --> 02:31.070
That hurt, dammit! You smacked too hard!

02:31.190 --> 02:32.440
S-Sakura!

02:32.670 --> 02:33.970
Do you know him?

02:36.170 --> 02:37.990
He was there on my first day here.

02:38.600 --> 02:41.680
You were all fired up
even before the term started!

02:41.940 --> 02:43.880
I figured they'd pick you!

02:44.100 --> 02:46.050
Quit makin' stuff up.

02:47.450 --> 02:48.770
…didn't you.

02:49.690 --> 02:51.330
Huh? What was that?

02:51.330 --> 02:52.630
S-Sakura!

02:53.050 --> 02:55.470
You also beat Togame, didn't you?

02:56.780 --> 02:57.680
Yeah.

02:57.780 --> 02:59.110
I-I heard it that time.

02:59.400 --> 03:01.500
Tamon's second-year rep's a repeater?

03:04.690 --> 03:07.340
Hey, you don't gotta do that stuff.

03:09.600 --> 03:11.800
And Sakura's the first-year rep?

03:13.590 --> 03:14.540
Countin' on ya.

03:15.220 --> 03:16.730
And you, too, Nirei and Suo.

03:17.240 --> 03:17.930
Thanks.

03:17.930 --> 03:19.430
Th-Th-Th-Th-Thank you!

03:19.790 --> 03:23.990
But if you ever run into any problems,
lay 'em on your upperclassmen.

03:24.680 --> 03:26.910
Your big bros'll do whatever they can!

03:30.250 --> 03:31.900
You three help 'em out, too!

03:32.130 --> 03:35.540
Tell 'em anything you wish
you'd done in your first years!

03:35.860 --> 03:36.630
Got it.

03:40.520 --> 03:41.560
What?

03:43.750 --> 03:45.860
Try to deal with things on your own.

03:46.410 --> 03:48.150
There's not much help I can give.

03:48.760 --> 03:51.190
I'm not your big bro, in the first place.

03:51.440 --> 03:52.710
I'm an only child.

03:53.110 --> 03:55.930
D-Dude, I already knew that.

03:56.280 --> 03:58.900
That's prrrobably not how he meant it.

03:59.010 --> 04:02.080
You're a role model now. Think before you speak.

04:10.630 --> 04:12.880
Oh! They're back, they're back!

04:13.590 --> 04:15.170
So, what wazzat about?

04:15.260 --> 04:17.590
A meet-and-greet with all the squads' reps!

04:17.780 --> 04:19.370
I was so moved!

04:19.450 --> 04:21.690
Huh?! Were the devas there, too?!

04:21.860 --> 04:23.120
Yep, they were.

04:23.310 --> 04:24.690
For reals?

04:24.950 --> 04:30.200
Must be nice! I'm dyin' to ask
the devas for their aesthetics!

04:30.330 --> 04:32.490
Right?! I want to know, too!

04:47.410 --> 04:49.660
Hey, man, we don't got patrols today,

04:49.780 --> 04:51.790
so wanna hit Muscle Power together?

04:51.790 --> 04:53.400
Ooh, good idea!

04:54.420 --> 04:55.730
- I'll pass.
- I'll pass.

04:59.560 --> 05:01.460
No good. He's not here.

05:02.670 --> 05:05.210
It'll be a problem if we go too far in.

05:05.530 --> 05:06.750
I know.

05:07.040 --> 05:08.690
You lookin' for something?

05:10.080 --> 05:11.500
If so, we'll help.

05:16.150 --> 05:18.390
Ah, man, thank goodness.

05:18.690 --> 05:21.500
We were just lookin' for you guys.

05:22.320 --> 05:23.320
But…

05:24.850 --> 05:27.210
You're not the ones.

05:30.470 --> 05:31.410
Later.

05:34.170 --> 05:37.010
Th-Those designs… Are they…?

05:37.480 --> 05:40.690
Mhm. White jackets with blue dragon bones.

05:41.270 --> 05:42.100
They're KEEL.

05:42.450 --> 05:44.710
KEEL? Who're they?

05:45.010 --> 05:46.550
I don't know the details,

05:47.160 --> 05:49.310
but I hear they're fairly small-scale.

05:49.880 --> 05:53.320
As you might guess from their vibe,
there are no good rumors.

05:53.620 --> 05:56.520
And those guys were lookin' for us?

05:56.680 --> 05:58.390
I don't know 'em.

05:58.790 --> 06:02.700
It sounded like they're probably
looking for someone from Furin, but…

06:05.260 --> 06:07.850
H-Hey, are you okay?!

06:07.940 --> 06:10.590
Dad! Get over here, Dad! There's trouble!

06:17.120 --> 06:18.500
Anzai?!

06:31.770 --> 06:33.920
Hey! Hey, you!

06:36.770 --> 06:39.300
Oh, thank goodness! You're awake!

06:39.720 --> 06:42.120
A-A-Are you okay, Anzai?!

06:42.340 --> 06:43.140
Uh…

06:43.200 --> 06:45.350
Come rest at my place for now.

06:45.810 --> 06:48.020
Ahhhh…

06:49.230 --> 06:53.770
Man, about that! A dog chased me!

06:54.080 --> 06:55.130
Huh?

06:55.570 --> 07:00.520
This dog as big as a bear was
chasing me, so I tried hiding there,

07:00.760 --> 07:03.000
and I was so relieved I passed out.

07:03.180 --> 07:06.840
Hey, Anzai, where can I find that bear?

07:06.940 --> 07:08.430
I wanna spar with it!

07:08.630 --> 07:10.490
It wasn't a bear, Tsuge.

07:10.670 --> 07:11.730
You.

07:11.860 --> 07:12.470
Huh?

07:12.800 --> 07:15.300
If you're gonna lie, come up with a better one.

07:15.640 --> 07:18.920
Right? It was so obvious even Sakura could tell.

07:18.980 --> 07:21.290
And Sakura believes everything!

07:21.420 --> 07:23.190
You two. Let's take this outside.

07:23.450 --> 07:25.950
No, man, it's really nothing.

07:26.410 --> 07:28.670
And I got stuff to do, so I'm out.

07:29.050 --> 07:31.430
Ma'am! I'll be back for some more monja!

07:31.740 --> 07:33.610
Hm?! You're already leaving?

07:33.930 --> 07:35.980
You can keep resting, you know.

07:36.110 --> 07:37.600
Naw, I'm fine.

07:37.860 --> 07:39.100
There we go.

07:40.100 --> 07:40.890
Anzai.

07:41.440 --> 07:42.970
Did KEEL do something to you?

07:47.800 --> 07:48.360
Wh…

07:48.960 --> 07:52.180
Wh-Wh-Wh-What are you talking about?

07:52.390 --> 07:54.420
It's way too obvious.

07:54.650 --> 07:56.900
[Draft beer (M)]
Oh, did you mean "beer"?!

07:56.990 --> 07:59.320
Please, I'm not even twenty yet!

07:59.550 --> 08:00.800
See you, ma'am!

08:01.000 --> 08:01.990
I'm heading out!

08:02.150 --> 08:03.500
See you guys later, too!

08:03.590 --> 08:05.710
Oh, if you're going, at least take…

08:06.040 --> 08:07.330
this… Ohh…

08:08.120 --> 08:11.100
I wanted to feed him some fresh ones.

08:11.690 --> 08:14.920
You Furin kids are always
helping and protecting us,

08:15.240 --> 08:17.430
so I can't express my thanks enough.

08:17.830 --> 08:20.140
You boys eat whatever you like, okay?

08:20.140 --> 08:21.210
Yaaay!

08:21.210 --> 08:24.070
For reals, lady?! I'll take cheese mentaiko mochi!

08:24.260 --> 08:26.210
Are you sure? We didn't do anything!

08:26.390 --> 08:27.980
What are you saying?

08:28.340 --> 08:32.620
You Furin boys are all like sons to me!

08:34.460 --> 08:39.350
Hey, Suo. How'd you figure out Anzai
had something to do with KEEL?

08:39.650 --> 08:42.310
I wasn't 100% sure,

08:42.830 --> 08:45.320
but given what that KEEL guy said,

08:45.450 --> 08:46.900
and the shape Anzai was in,

08:47.140 --> 08:49.650
I thought there might be a connection.

08:50.330 --> 08:51.190
And, well,

08:51.640 --> 08:52.990
seems I was right.

08:54.330 --> 08:55.210
Sakura!

08:55.460 --> 08:56.520
What do we do?

08:56.630 --> 08:57.280
Huh?

08:57.450 --> 08:59.240
If Suo's right about this,

08:59.460 --> 09:02.130
then KEEL are the ones who hurt Anzai!

09:02.520 --> 09:05.120
That means we have to save him, Sakura!

09:05.240 --> 09:06.850
He's our classmate!

09:06.990 --> 09:10.920
Wait, hold on a sec!
Even if those KEEL guys got him,

09:11.030 --> 09:12.400
he didn't say a word!

09:13.130 --> 09:16.330
That means he's got his own thoughts about it,

09:17.050 --> 09:20.490
and we don't know if he even wants us to save him.

09:20.930 --> 09:22.210
B-But…

09:22.770 --> 09:24.050
Everyone…

09:24.970 --> 09:27.760
has a thing or two they don't wanna talk about.

09:31.410 --> 09:36.300
B-But even so, we're in the same
class now! We're friends!

09:36.930 --> 09:40.730
Don't you want to at least try to help him?!

09:41.610 --> 09:43.940
Watch over and help them!

09:44.520 --> 09:45.330
Tch.

09:49.080 --> 09:50.010
I'm leaving.

09:50.130 --> 09:53.560
What?! Wait, Sakura, we still need to talk!

09:53.800 --> 09:55.970
Oh, you're leaving, too?

09:56.360 --> 09:58.180
Then take this with you!

10:02.870 --> 10:04.260
That Sakura…

10:04.540 --> 10:06.740
He's not very honest, huh?

10:07.030 --> 10:09.890
Not with himself, and not with us.

10:11.210 --> 10:13.190
He's missin' out on the monja!

10:14.710 --> 10:15.540
Nire.

10:16.030 --> 10:17.020
It'll be okay.

10:19.460 --> 10:21.030
Hey, are you okay?!

10:21.470 --> 10:23.490
Was this their doing, too?

10:24.810 --> 10:26.650
This is nothing.

10:28.020 --> 10:29.010
And Nagato?

10:31.670 --> 10:32.710
It was no good.

10:34.130 --> 10:35.690
I couldn't bring him back.

10:37.740 --> 10:39.840
That team's seriously bad news.

10:40.420 --> 10:41.930
At this rate, Nagato…

10:42.680 --> 10:45.160
he'll cross a line of no return.

10:47.620 --> 10:51.240
Hey, I think maybe it's time we asked Furin to…

10:51.240 --> 10:52.480
We can't do that!

10:53.870 --> 10:54.820
I'm sorry.

10:55.700 --> 10:57.120
But we can't.

10:57.300 --> 10:57.750
[East Wind Shopping Street]

10:57.750 --> 10:58.950
[East Wind Shopping Street]
Furin is…

10:58.950 --> 10:59.790
[East Wind Shopping Street]

10:59.790 --> 11:00.910
[East Wind Shopping Street]
Bofurin is…

11:00.910 --> 11:02.040
[East Wind Shopping Street]

11:02.040 --> 11:04.250
a team dedicated to protecting the town.

11:05.540 --> 11:07.860
This is my own personal problem.

11:08.420 --> 11:09.950
I can't rope them in.

11:10.120 --> 11:10.680
Huh?

11:11.670 --> 11:13.830
Then I'll go with you next time!

11:14.410 --> 11:17.050
Don't be stupid! It's too dangerous!

11:25.670 --> 11:28.070
It's okay. Leave it to me.

11:30.470 --> 11:32.210
I'll get it done by myself.

11:39.650 --> 11:43.290
What part of that face is okay?

11:44.520 --> 11:46.070
You're so beat up…

11:47.850 --> 11:49.930
How is that okay?

11:51.540 --> 11:52.230
Hey.

11:53.730 --> 11:54.980
I overheard.

11:55.820 --> 11:57.130
Give me details.

12:00.700 --> 12:02.810
Wh-Who…

12:03.380 --> 12:04.330
are you…?

12:04.880 --> 12:07.110
One of that guy's classmates.

12:07.910 --> 12:09.980
Tell me about what you talked about.

12:19.690 --> 12:23.410
A-Anzai and I are childhood friends,

12:23.690 --> 12:27.000
and we played in this park all the time as kids.

12:27.690 --> 12:29.910
And at some point along the line,

12:30.280 --> 12:32.060
a boy named Nagato joined us.

12:32.870 --> 12:36.380
Anzai and I were rowdy, and often
went too far and got hurt.

12:37.220 --> 12:39.750
Nagato was well-behaved and gentle,

12:39.930 --> 12:42.980
but always stuck with us through everything.

12:43.740 --> 12:46.630
We all split up into different high schools,

12:47.030 --> 12:50.580
but we thought we'd all stay good friends.

12:51.400 --> 12:52.250
But then…

12:53.380 --> 12:55.560
Oh, hey! Is that Anzai I spy?

12:55.980 --> 13:00.380
Long time no see! Though I guess
it hasn't been that long since graduation.

13:01.530 --> 13:04.890
Ah, look at that face. You get in another fight?

13:05.320 --> 13:06.980
You never change.

13:07.380 --> 13:10.300
Nagato'd be disappointed.
He'd be all, "What, again?"

13:11.120 --> 13:13.450
Now I wanna see him again, too!

13:16.090 --> 13:19.700
I got this when a team called KEEL jumped me.

13:20.010 --> 13:20.860
KEEL?

13:21.590 --> 13:25.390
I saw one of them trying to snatch a purse today,

13:25.930 --> 13:27.340
and tried to stop him.

13:27.780 --> 13:29.310
It wasn't inside this town,

13:29.990 --> 13:31.910
but I couldn't just ignore it.

13:32.980 --> 13:34.040
I grabbed his arm,

13:34.900 --> 13:36.870
and pulled his hood down.

13:37.820 --> 13:38.920
And when I did…

13:39.890 --> 13:41.300
Who do you think it was?

13:46.670 --> 13:49.240
It was… Nagato.

13:49.880 --> 13:52.690
Nagato wasn't the type to do that sort of thing!

13:53.130 --> 13:56.500
So today, Anzai went to try to bring Nagato here,

13:56.710 --> 13:58.630
so we could hear his side, but…

13:59.610 --> 14:03.160
He came back alone, and all beat up.

14:04.200 --> 14:06.930
When I asked him why, he didn't give any details,

14:07.400 --> 14:08.940
and he says it's dangerous,

14:09.140 --> 14:12.470
and it's a personal problem,
so he won't rope Furin in.

14:12.890 --> 14:15.190
He's trying to deal with it on his own!

14:16.230 --> 14:18.420
That's why he didn't say anything to us?

14:22.600 --> 14:24.960
Wh-Wh-Why are you crying?

14:25.880 --> 14:28.120
My childhood friend is having a hard time,

14:28.920 --> 14:30.230
and I can't do anything.

14:31.200 --> 14:34.680
All I can do is wait, and it's frustrating.

14:35.970 --> 14:38.650
I'm frustrated with how powerless I am!

14:43.860 --> 14:44.880
Got it.

14:45.610 --> 14:48.890
So I just gotta drag that Nagato guy here, yeah?

14:49.290 --> 14:49.880
Huh?

14:50.460 --> 14:55.750
But Anzai said Furin was dedicated to protecting
the town, and he couldn't rope them in.

14:56.210 --> 14:58.710
Well, that's, uh, it'll work out!

14:59.080 --> 15:00.600
I'm his classmate,

15:00.820 --> 15:02.770
and I'm stronger than you.

15:03.920 --> 15:06.920
You can just say, "Leave it to me."

15:07.740 --> 15:09.660
S-So, uh…

15:11.590 --> 15:13.510
L-Leave it to me.

15:19.270 --> 15:21.050
You're a pretty good guy, huh?

15:23.460 --> 15:24.470
Thank you.

15:26.190 --> 15:29.720
Y-You were crying, so I had no choice, is all!

15:31.030 --> 15:33.210
That's all the more reason to thank you!

15:34.630 --> 15:38.000
All this relief is making me
realize how hungry I am.

15:38.380 --> 15:40.070
Huh? I ain't givin' you any.

15:40.470 --> 15:41.000
Eh?

15:41.450 --> 15:43.750
Oh. Okay. I didn't want it.

15:49.010 --> 15:50.890
I said all that,

15:51.570 --> 15:53.270
but what do I do now?

15:55.130 --> 15:57.350
- Oh, mornin', Sakura!
- Morniiing.

15:57.350 --> 15:58.150
Morning.

15:58.150 --> 15:59.300
Good morning!

16:00.020 --> 16:02.180
Naw, man, I'm tellin' the truth!

16:02.340 --> 16:05.950
I was grapplin' with a bear,
and barely managed to get away!

16:06.070 --> 16:09.080
Liar. Who got you?

16:09.210 --> 16:10.960
Lay it on us. We won't laugh.

16:11.810 --> 16:13.620
It doesn't matter what you say,

16:14.130 --> 16:16.130
he'll just dance around it.

16:19.270 --> 16:20.170
Sakura,

16:20.500 --> 16:22.460
did you talk to Anzai yesterday?

16:22.680 --> 16:25.310
Huh? Huh?! What are you talking about?!

16:25.470 --> 16:28.380
You're easy to read, too, Sakura.

16:29.510 --> 16:31.660
Oi. Is Anzai here?

16:32.030 --> 16:32.950
Right here!

16:33.100 --> 16:34.020
What's up?

16:34.550 --> 16:35.270
Hey.

16:35.740 --> 16:36.490
Who's that?

16:36.630 --> 16:39.350
He's Tochimoto, from Class 4.

16:40.790 --> 16:42.660
What's this? A love letter?

16:42.810 --> 16:45.190
Love letters don't come in brown envelopes.

16:45.740 --> 16:49.450
Someone stopped me on my way
to school and said to deliver that.

16:50.000 --> 16:53.990
Dude had a hood on and creeped me right out.

17:07.500 --> 17:09.260
Ah! Anzai?!

17:10.280 --> 17:11.660
Eh?! Sakura?!

17:13.880 --> 17:14.920
Hey, wait!

17:15.400 --> 17:16.690
I said wait!

17:24.790 --> 17:25.990
Damn you…

17:27.050 --> 17:27.990
Wait!

17:29.770 --> 17:30.640
What?!

17:31.000 --> 17:31.840
Move!

17:31.960 --> 17:35.320
I talked to the girl who was
with you in the park yesterday.

17:35.890 --> 17:37.770
Huh?! Why'd you talk to Tsuchiya?!

17:38.070 --> 17:39.760
That doesn't matter right now.

17:40.230 --> 17:41.830
That's from KEEL, right?

17:44.070 --> 17:44.810
Hey!

17:45.100 --> 17:45.700
Wait!

17:48.270 --> 17:49.130
Tch.

17:49.130 --> 17:50.050
[Nagato's all beat up. Waaah!]

17:50.050 --> 17:51.200
[Nagato's all beat up. Waaah!]
Scumbags.

17:51.200 --> 17:53.000
[We're waiting at the old Senkan shipyard!!]

17:53.210 --> 17:54.870
It has nothing to do with you!

17:58.320 --> 17:59.450
What now?!

18:02.180 --> 18:04.350
Tell me about it, Anzai.

18:09.380 --> 18:10.820
It happened two days ago.

18:17.300 --> 18:19.510
I saw a purse-snatcher.

18:20.410 --> 18:21.590
So I caught him,

18:22.200 --> 18:24.020
and took his hood off.

18:26.060 --> 18:27.140
He was…

18:28.060 --> 18:31.030
my childhood friend, Nagato.

18:34.040 --> 18:37.590
He punched me, tossed the bag, and ran.

18:38.320 --> 18:41.800
So I went back there yesterday.

18:42.800 --> 18:45.930
I had to find out what happened to him.

18:51.540 --> 18:54.850
Come on, you know this ain't enough.

18:55.240 --> 18:58.830
Pretty sure I said the same to you before, too.

18:58.830 --> 19:00.580
I-I'm sorry…

19:00.670 --> 19:04.300
Now we're in a bind. But if you
don't got it, you don't got it.

19:04.870 --> 19:07.200
Guess it's time to give you more.

19:07.590 --> 19:09.300
One punch is a thousand yen,

19:09.420 --> 19:13.210
so I'll hit you ten times and
we'll say you brought ten grand.

19:13.940 --> 19:14.900
Here we go.

19:15.140 --> 19:16.590
A thousand yen!

19:16.820 --> 19:18.560
Two thousand yen!

19:18.750 --> 19:20.600
Three thousand yen!

19:27.730 --> 19:29.220
What's this, then?

19:34.100 --> 19:36.020
Let's go, Nagato! Now!

19:42.170 --> 19:44.930
What do you think you're doing?

19:45.480 --> 19:46.660
What do you mean…?

19:49.960 --> 19:50.990
This has…

19:51.510 --> 19:53.100
nothing to do with you.

19:55.780 --> 19:57.180
I made my choice.

19:58.270 --> 19:59.700
I chose to be here.

20:05.020 --> 20:08.210
So please just mind your own business!

20:14.100 --> 20:16.890
I somehow managed to get to the shopping street,

20:17.650 --> 20:19.030
and you know the rest.

20:19.690 --> 20:23.000
But he's staying with them
after they were so shitty to him?

20:23.500 --> 20:24.620
What's that about?

20:25.130 --> 20:26.280
I don't know.

20:27.080 --> 20:29.170
But he…

20:30.060 --> 20:31.140
was crying.

20:32.010 --> 20:33.820
When I broke a leg roughhousing,

20:34.170 --> 20:36.410
or got lost and couldn't get back home,

20:36.780 --> 20:39.370
Nagato was always polite and kind.

20:39.870 --> 20:41.360
He was strong.

20:42.020 --> 20:43.840
I don't know what happened,

20:44.610 --> 20:46.590
but he was crying.

20:47.220 --> 20:49.100
That's reason enough.

20:50.710 --> 20:52.000
I'm going to…

20:54.480 --> 20:56.080
pull him out of there!

20:58.170 --> 20:59.180
I see.

21:00.200 --> 21:01.020
Let's go.

21:02.370 --> 21:04.650
Wh-Why are you going?

21:05.210 --> 21:07.000
This is a personal problem!

21:07.370 --> 21:10.320
Besides, those guys are seriously bad news!

21:10.700 --> 21:12.130
I can't rope you…

21:12.870 --> 21:14.220
can't rope Furin in!

21:14.220 --> 21:15.560
The hell do you mean?

21:16.410 --> 21:18.610
It doesn't matter who they are.

21:19.260 --> 21:21.540
And I'm not going as a member of Furin.

21:22.760 --> 21:25.480
I made a promise to that girl.

21:26.280 --> 21:28.600
Said I'd drag that Nagato guy out.

21:29.380 --> 21:30.580
Rope me in?

21:31.380 --> 21:34.120
Don't talk like you're who this is about.

21:35.830 --> 21:37.580
This is my problem.

21:39.610 --> 21:42.710
Gotcha. So that's what happened.

21:51.520 --> 21:52.540
Guys…

21:53.240 --> 21:54.120
Why are you all…

21:54.410 --> 21:57.500
First yesterday, then just now…

21:57.890 --> 22:00.500
You gotta get better at hiding stuff.

22:00.580 --> 22:02.210
Don't be so distant.

22:02.620 --> 22:04.490
Why didn't you say anything?

22:05.210 --> 22:07.160
Well, I mean…

22:08.030 --> 22:10.580
Furin's about protecting the town.

22:11.000 --> 22:14.680
I ain't here 'cause I'm Furin, though.

22:15.100 --> 22:19.530
Not savin' a guy who's in trouble
ain't my aesthetic.

22:19.700 --> 22:22.610
He's right! I wanted to help, too!

22:23.850 --> 22:25.480
It's like they said.

22:25.880 --> 22:28.040
We just wanted to help a pal.

22:34.540 --> 22:35.580
Guys…

22:36.720 --> 22:40.220
Come on. If you don't hurry,
they'll leave without you.

22:41.260 --> 22:43.530
I'm sorry I woke you, but…

22:44.260 --> 22:47.910
If just one of us didn't help
with a classmate's major problem,

22:48.280 --> 22:51.000
it would probably make Umemiya sad.

22:51.840 --> 22:54.220
So Sugishita says he'll come, too!

23:01.380 --> 23:02.350
What is it?

23:03.370 --> 23:04.280
Wha?!

23:04.540 --> 23:06.740
What do they think they'rrre doing?!

23:08.790 --> 23:10.490
So where was the place again?

23:10.560 --> 23:13.480
Hmm, I think he said the old Senkan shipyard.

23:13.690 --> 23:16.170
So that's KEEL's base?

23:16.980 --> 23:21.090
Judging by the picture,
we don't have time to waste.

23:21.560 --> 23:22.510
I know.

23:26.970 --> 23:29.970
[#13: For a Friend]

23:32.540 --> 23:33.250
Oi.

23:33.650 --> 23:35.480
Say what you will, but I'm going.

23:36.000 --> 23:37.490
I'm his friend, too!

23:39.670 --> 23:41.010
Keep up.

23:42.500 --> 23:43.340
I will!
